+# Breaking changes
+
+## Scope
+
+Commits `c659a45dfac38cbc74391b32a465ae5c12121a34` and `d95b8ca1b4b80e2501a543560d031ba4ac94a3db` replace the v3 error snapshot with classic v4 errors and add v4 core error definitions. `sources/upstream.json` still identifies `zod@3.25.76`. This is an API-export change, not evidence of a new package release. This package provides v3 through `zod` and `zod/v3`, and classic v4 through `zod/v4`.
+
+## Validation issue property
+
+Previously, v3 `ZodError.errors` was a getter returning `this.issues`. In the v4 snapshot, `.issues` remains but `.errors` is absent; the upstream observation records `.errors` as undefined.
+
+Replace `error.errors` with `error.issues` in logging, iteration, serialization, and assertions, including `result.error.issues` after a failed `safeParse`. Keep the failure guard. This property also exists in v3, so handlers can adopt it before switching imports. The v4 core makes `.issues` non-enumerable: explicitly include it in structured output instead of relying on object spreading.
+
+## Issue shapes and custom maps
+
+Audit issue consumers against `sources/zod-core-errors.ts`:
+
+| Previous v3 shape | New v4 shape | Migration |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `invalid_union.unionErrors`: `ZodError[]` | `invalid_union.errors`: issue arrays | Iterate nested arrays directly instead of reading each nested error's `.issues`. |
+| `invalid_string.validation` | `invalid_format.format`, plus format-specific fields | Update switches and field reads. |
+| `invalid_literal` and `invalid_enum_value` | `invalid_value` with `values` | Handle the consolidated code and allowed-value array. |
+| `too_small.type` / `too_big.type` | `origin` | Rename reads; `inclusive` is now optional. |
+| `not_multiple_of.multipleOf` | `divisor` | Rename field reads. |
+| `invalid_type.received` | No `received` field in the new interface | Remove reliance on that field. |
+| Paths of `(string \| number)[]` | `PropertyKey[]` | Allow symbol segments in path consumers. |
+
+The new union includes `invalid_key` and `invalid_element`, each with nested `issues`. Old codes including `invalid_arguments`, `invalid_return_type`, `invalid_date`, `invalid_intersection_types`, `invalid_union_discriminator`, and `not_finite` are absent from the new union. Update exhaustive switches. The error snapshots alone do not establish which replacement issue every schema or parser emits.
+
+The old `ZodErrorMap` accepted an issue and a context containing `defaultError` and `data`, returning `{ message }`. The new alias points to `$ZodErrorMap`, which takes one raw issue and can return `{ message }`, a string, `undefined`, or `null`. Rewrite callbacks to the one-argument contract. The new snapshot does not export `ErrorMapCtx`. `IssueData` now aliases `$ZodRawIssue`; update annotations rather than assuming the old `fatal` contract.
+
+## Error helpers
+
+The v3 `formErrors` getter is absent from the new classic interface. Use the retained `.flatten()` method for the `formErrors` / `fieldErrors` shape, or migrate to a core utility. `.format()` and `.flatten()` remain but are deprecated; the source recommends `z.treeifyError(error)`. Its `errors` / `properties` / `items` tree has a different shape, so update consumers when adopting it.
+
+Replace deprecated `.addIssue()` and `.addIssues()` with pushes to `.issues`, and `.isEmpty` with `.issues.length === 0`. Previously the add methods replaced the array; now they mutate it in place. Review retained array references. The new core defines `.issues` without a writable flag: mutate the array rather than reassigning it.
+
+The old class explicitly extended `Error`; the new snapshot uses constructor helpers and separately defines `ZodRealError` with `Parent: Error`. The committed snapshots omit the constructor-helper and parser implementations, so they do not alone prove `instanceof Error` behavior for every parse result. Verify dependencies on this behavior with the selected runtime.
+
+After migrating imports and handlers, verify failing parses, nested union issues, custom maps, and formatted-error consumers with the selected v4 runtime. See [Error handling](/guides/errors) for the corrected minimal example.
